    <string name="help_install">Install on both devices</string>
    <string name="help_install_body">Install N2 Launcher on your phone and watch. Both apps must have the same package and signature. After pairing, open the watch app once and tap Refresh on this phone.</string>
    <string name="help_home">Use it as your home screen</string>
    <string name="help_home_body">On your watch, open Settings → Apps → Default apps → Home app and choose N2 Launcher, if available. Some watches do not allow replacing the home screen. Use the N2 Launcher Tile or its app icon instead.</string>
    <string name="help_pair">Before syncing</string>
    <string name="help_pair_body">Pair your watch through its Wear OS companion app. Keep Bluetooth or Wi-Fi connected, enable Google Play services, and install N2 Launcher on both devices. “Sent” means the phone published your draft; “Applied” means the watch confirmed it.</string>
    <string name="help_offline">Can I edit offline?</string>
    <string name="help_offline_body">Yes. Your draft and icons are saved on this phone. Reconnect, refresh and sync when ready. Demo mode is separate and never syncs.</string>
    <string name="help_conflict">What if I edited on my watch too?</string>
    <string name="help_conflict_body">N2 warns you before replacing newer watch changes. Load the watch configuration to keep its edits, or explicitly overwrite it with your phone draft.</string>
    <string name="help_icons">Which icon packs work?</string>
    <string name="help_icons_body">ZIPs with package-named images (com.example.app.png) and common appfilter.xml component mappings. Non-image files and unsafe paths are rejected. Review matches before applying. Photo selection needs no storage permission.</string>
    <string name="help_privacy">Your data stays with you</string>
    <string name="help_privacy_body">Drafts and images stay on your phone and paired watch. N2 does not upload them to a server. Usage-based sorting uses launches recorded by the watch launcher, not Android-wide usage access.</string>
